= The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> breaks with the coalition

<img src="img/Kollwitz_Arbeitslosigkeit.jpg" style="display:block; width:100%; max-width:500px; height:auto; margin:0 auto 1em auto; object-fit:cover; object-position:top;">

Following a sharp rise in unemployment after Black Thursday, the unemployment insurance fund has been overstretched and is on the verge of insolvency. To ensure that the unemployed still receive their welfare cheques, we have worked out a compromise with the other centrist parties, in which contribution rates would increase and welfare would have a small cut. However, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**ADGB**</span> and the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD's**</span> intransigent left wing have rejected our compromise and pressured the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD's**</span> national leadership to reject this offer and leave the government.
Originally, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD's**</span> presence in government has been tolerated due to the need for their support for the Young Plan. With the recent ratification of the Young Plan, <span style="color: #808080;">Hindenburg</span> sees no reason to persuade the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> to remain in government. 

