title: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> ends their toleration of the [+ chancellor +] cabinet

With the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD's**</span> exit, the current government no longer holds a majority in the Reichstag and a new cabinet must take its place. Due to Bruning's Christian Nationalist outlook and commitment to fiscal discipline, <span style="color: #808080;">Hindenburg</span> views him as an acceptable candidate for Chancellor and entrusts to him with the mandate to broker a cabinet. Now, all we can do is wait and see whether he can survive the vote of no confidence next month.
